  "details": "6-pt tracking breaks locomotion of generic avatar until the user switches back to an humanoid avatar.\nTo reproduce:\n- In open beta 1084\n- Spawn in an Humanoid avatar\n- Enable 6-pt tracking\n- Hit Calibrate\n- Calibrate onto the Humanoid avatar\n- Switch to a Generic avatar\nObserved:\n- FBT calibration is prompted in the generic avatar\n- The quick menu is very small\n- After \"calibrating\", the generic avatar is stuck in place cannot be locomoted around with the joystick\n- Switching back to an humanoid avatar allows locomotion\nExpected:\n- No calibration is prompted for\n- The generic avatar should be locomotable\n--------------\n4-pt tracking breaks locomotion of generic avatar until the user switches to another world.\n- In open beta 1084\n- Spawn in an Humanoid avatar\n- Enable 4-pt tracking (hip only)\n- Hit Calibrate\n- Calibrate onto the Humanoid avatar\n- Switch to a Generic avatar\nObserved:\n- FBT calibration is prompted in the generic avatar\n- The quick menu is very small\n- It is impossible to \"calibrate\", the balls always stay\n- Switching back to an humanoid avatar still does not allow locomotion, the humanoid avatar is stuck in place cannot be locomoted around with the joystick\n- Rejoining a new world allows locomotion again\nExpected:\n- No calibration is prompted for\n- The generic avatar should be locomotable",
